# CQROS Quantitative Research Rules

## Identity

CQROS is a quantitative research platform.

Research quality always has higher priority than implementation speed.

Never optimize for convenience at the expense of scientific validity.

---

# Scientific Method

Every research task follows

Question

↓

Hypothesis

↓

Dataset

↓

Feature Engineering

↓

Target Generation

↓

Statistical Validation

↓

Walk Forward Validation

↓

Stress Testing

↓

Approval

↓

Production

Never skip a stage.

---

# Reproducibility

Every experiment must be reproducible.

Record

Dataset Version

Dataset Hash

Feature Version

Target Version

Policy Version

Configuration Version

Random Seed

Git Commit

Container Version

Python Version

Library Versions

Execution Timestamp

Researcher

Nothing is anonymous.

---

# Dataset Rules

Research datasets must be

Immutable

Versioned

Timestamp aligned

Leakage free

Schema validated

Lineage tracked

Research Ready

Never modify datasets in-place.

---

# Feature Engineering

Every feature requires metadata.

Feature metadata includes

Name

Description

Formula

Dependencies

Window

Normalization

Expected Range

Missing Value Policy

Version

Creator

Validation Status

Deprecation Status

---

# Feature Health

Every feature continuously tracks

Missing Rate

Distribution Drift

Population Stability Index

Correlation Drift

Regime Stability

Update Frequency

Production Health

Automatically deprecate unstable features.

---

# Feature Approval

A feature cannot be promoted unless

Leakage Score = 0

Validation Passed

Metadata Complete

Version Assigned

Statistical Significance Verified

---

# Target Rules

Targets must

Look only forward

Never overlap improperly

Be timestamp aligned

Support multiple horizons

Support volatility adjustment

Support regime evaluation

Never use future information.

---

# Leakage Prevention

Zero tolerance.

Validate

Timestamp Leakage

Window Leakage

Target Leakage

Label Leakage

Feature Leakage

Cross Dataset Leakage

Metadata Leakage

If leakage exists

STOP.

Reject the dataset.

---

# Statistical Validation

Every factor reports

IC

Rank IC

Newey-West t-stat

Bootstrap Confidence

Effective Sample Size

Sharpe

Sortino

Trade Count

Turnover

Capacity

Drawdown

Tail Risk

Never promote a factor without statistics.

---

# Promotion Thresholds

Every strategy family defines configurable minimums.

Examples

Minimum IC

Minimum Rank IC

Minimum ESS

Minimum Trade Count

Minimum OOS Sharpe

Minimum t-stat

Thresholds belong in Policy Content.

Never hardcode them.

---

# Regime Awareness

All statistics are computed

Overall

Bull

Bear

Sideways

High Volatility

Low Volatility

Liquidity Stress

Panic

Recovery

Classify research as

Regime Robust

Regime Limited

Regime Specific

---

# Walk Forward

Research approval requires

Rolling windows

Multiple periods

Multiple market conditions

Multiple assets

No random train/test split for time series.

---

# Cross Validation

Use

Rolling Validation

Expanding Window

Anchored Walk Forward

Purged CV

Embargo CV

Never use standard K-Fold for time series.

---

# Model Evaluation

Measure

Prediction Quality

Calibration

Stability

Turnover

Capacity

Execution Cost

Regime Performance

Uncertainty

Confidence

---

# Experiment Tracking

Every experiment records

Objective

Hypothesis

Dataset

Features

Targets

Configuration

Parameters

Models

Metrics

Artifacts

Approval Status

Reviewer

Comments

Nothing is lost.

---

# Research Governance

Research states

Draft

Running

Validated

Approved

Rejected

Archived

Deprecated

Production

Every transition is recorded.

---

# AI Rules

Never claim statistical significance without evidence.

Never ignore leakage.

Never use future data.

Never approve research with incomplete metadata.

Never bypass validation.

If uncertainty exists,

stop and explain why.

---

# Completion

Research is complete only when

✓ Dataset Validated

✓ Leakage Free

✓ Metadata Complete

✓ Features Validated

✓ Targets Validated

✓ Statistics Generated

✓ Walk Forward Completed

✓ Stress Tests Passed

✓ Governance Approved

✓ Documentation Updated

Only then may research move toward production.